<title>USA: Texas Utilities shareholders okay deal.</title>
<headline>Texas Utilities shareholders okay deal.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texas Utilities Co president Erle Nye said shareholders approved on Friday at a special meeting the $1.7 billion purchase of ENSERCH Corp.</p>
<p>Under the deal, Texas Utilities will acquire ENSERCH's distribution and pipeline companies, Lone Star Gas and Lone Star Pipeline, with about $550 million of Texas Utilities common stock and $1.15 billion in debt and preferred stock.</p>
<p>ENSERCH Corp shareholders were to vote on the merger deal later Friday. If approved, ENSERCH Corp will spin off its 83 percent-owned exploration and production company, ENSERCH Exploration Inc.</p>
</text>
